From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:48:48 +0200
Subject: wifi: brcmfmac: ignore P2P probe requests without a P2P interface

BCM4330 firmware (AP6330) reports P2P probe requests from nearby devices
when no P2P interface exists. Each one logs two errors, about ten lines per
minute. Ignore these events, and log them at debug level.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fweh.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fweh.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fweh.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fweh.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fweh.c
@@ -313,6 +313,13 @@ static void brcmf_fweh_event_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 			ifp = drvr->iflist[0];
 		else
 			ifp = drvr->iflist[emsg.bsscfgidx];
+
+		/* Some firmware reports probe requests without a P2P interface. */
+		if (!ifp && event->code == BRCMF_E_P2P_PROBEREQ_MSG) {
+			brcmf_dbg(EVENT, "no P2P interface, probe request ignored\n");
+			goto event_free;
+		}
+
 		err = brcmf_fweh_call_event_handler(drvr, ifp, event->code,
 						    &emsg, event->data);
 		if (err) {
-- 
